  urldate = {2022-10-07},
  abstract = {Oxygen consumption, carbon dioxide production, and respiratory rate decrease during the practice of a new, easilylearned relaxation technique. The elements of the technique are a mental device to prevent distracting thoughts, a passive attitude, decreased muscle tonus, and a quiet environment which is as free of visual and auditory stimuli as possible. Sitting quietly with either the eyes open or closed failed to produce the same changes. These physiologic changes are consistent with an integrated hypothalamic response, recently termed the "relaxation response," which results in hypothesized decreased sympathetic activity. Regular elicitation of the relaxation response may be of therapeutic value in diseases characterized by increased sympathetic nervous system activity.},
