  abstract = {This paper exploits the implied information of data collected from\textbackslash ncredit spreads of Chinese corporate bonds and systemic and idiosyncratic\textbackslash nrisk factors. We compute contribution of risk factors to credit spreads\textbackslash nof Chinese corporate bonds by establishing the unbalanced panel data\textbackslash nmodel, identify the key factors impacting the size of credit spreads of\textbackslash ncorporate bonds. Knowledge extracted by data mining is helpful to\textbackslash ninvestors for reasonable pricing of bonds and making rational investment\textbackslash ndecisions. When selecting variables, the unbalanced panel data model is\textbackslash nused to calculate the Zero-volatility credit spreads, which are more\textbackslash naccurate. We use term structure adjusted return of bond index as the\textbackslash nsystemic risk factor of corporate bond market, the three Fama/French\textbackslash nsystemic factors as the systemic risk factors of stock markets and\textbackslash nidiosyncratic stock/bond volatility and idiosyncratic bond value-at-risk\textbackslash nas the idiosyncratic risk factors. Empirical analysis of corporate bonds\textbackslash nsampling China's listing Corporation issued and traded on Shanghai Stock\textbackslash nExchange from 2008 to 2011 shows that the size of credit spreads is\textbackslash nmainly determined by the systemic risk factors of bond market, i.e. risk\textbackslash nfactors of stock market make very little contribution to the spread; the\textbackslash nidiosyncratic risk factors also contribute. An interesting phenomenon is\textbackslash nthat we find that the relationship between idiosyncratic stock\textbackslash nvolatility and credit spread is negative, which is contrary to extant\textbackslash nresearch while the relationship is positive and mainly focuses on impact\textbackslash nof risk factors on credit spread of corporate bond.},
